{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "id": "h200-contiguous-mqa-epilogue-001",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The supplied installed excerpt contains \"fmaxf(shifted_accum[j], 0)\" and both uncompensated scale multiplications, establishing a concrete source delta. Replacing the epilogue instruction could reduce exposed contiguous-prefill time. The proposed cheap include/JIT/dispatch inspection addresses deployment eligibility before implementation. Equally compiled and warmed stock code is an appropriate simple comparator. Actual invocation and bottleneck exposure remain unknown; measuring them is a legitimate first falsification step."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The matching SM90 header and author-reported H200 tests support a plausible narrow port. However, active artifact provenance and a sufficient numerical-domain invariant remain unknown. The author's \"bit-exact numerics\" assertion is not generally valid: intermediate doubling can overflow, scale halving can underflow, and exceptional-value behavior differs. The proposal correctly acknowledges these issues and specifies reference, top-k, graph/cache, distributed and quality checks, but their outcomes and applicable G01–G05 definitions are unavailable."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The design specifies patched hits over independently identified eligible calls, all-rank coverage, cache-controlled negative controls, competing explanations, native anchors, separate diagnostics and held-out conditions. It preserves the required stage order, TPOT definition, unprofiled frontier and at least five alternating paired full-run confirmation blocks. Support/reject/inconclusive rules are meaningful. Practical-effect thresholds, numerical/quality tolerances, tail guardrails, adequate coverage and a maximum experiment budget still need operational definitions."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 5,
          "rationale": "Observed evidence is supplied source text, not measured execution. DeepGEMM #452 includes before/after code and author claims of H200 gains: \"avg +3.7%\" and selected-shape timing using \"best of 3 reps\". The draft correctly treats lower serving TTFT as transfer inference. It challenges universal exactness and records missing distributions, worst-case regressions, CP meaning and the 8K case's D as unknown. The #303 slowdown anecdote is appropriately contextualized; neither its cause nor closure rationale establishes rejection of #452."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "A conditional three-line header port offers inexpensive initial falsification and straightforward source rollback, although JIT artifact isolation must also be verified. Cold/warm discrimination addresses whether native prefix-heavy traffic exposes useful work. The proposal avoids claiming direct paged-decode gains and keeps eight-GPU node pricing parameterized. Integration effort and serving benefit remain unknown. Its prefill mechanism complements decode and routing directions, but five-selection portfolio coverage cannot be established from one submitted hypothesis."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "An unchanged installed header does not prove the serving process executes it. Include resolution, loaded dependencies, JIT cache provenance and eligible invocation coverage must establish the effective baseline.",
        "Finite accumulator observations alone cannot qualify the arithmetic. Bounds must cover doubled accumulators, weighted products, intermediate reductions and halved scales under actual compiler rounding and flush-to-zero behavior. The scalar overflow counterexample challenges universal equivalence; it does not establish a failure on reachable deployment inputs.",
        "The highlighted 8K author benchmark uses BF16 logits. Supplied vLLM #61149 states \"SM90 and SM120 keep the FP8 format, FP32 weights and FP32 logits.\" That is an attributed branch-description claim, not proof of pinned deployment membership, but it makes dtype and compressed-row API matching an explicit transfer question.",
        "Kernel throughput gains cannot establish primary-workload TTFT or goodput gains. Prefix reuse, other prefill stages and contention may remove the exposed benefit; the proposed controls appropriately test these alternatives.",
        "The experiment's decision thresholds and stopping budget remain unspecified. Five paired blocks are a minimum design requirement, not assurance that a small effect will be resolved."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Retain as a deferred inspection candidate, not a qualified deployment selection. The weighted score is 78/100, but the unknown required applicability/correctness gate prevents qualification. Before a later bounded experiment, document the active artifact and shape/dtype/API mapping, establish an enforceable numerical eligibility domain or retain stock behavior, and predeclare correctness tolerances, practical-effect and regression thresholds, activation coverage and stopping limits. No demonstrated speedup is required before that experiment."
    }
  ],
  "global_gaps": [
    "Only one hypothesis was submitted. The rubric's five-selection portfolio objective and comprehensive thirteen-repository research coverage cannot be assessed from this review packet.",
    "No independent GPU measurements, active dispatch traces or serving effects are supplied. The packet does contain relevant engineering excerpts; missing execution evidence does not negate their source-level support.",
    "G01–G05 definitions, production H200 SLOs and node price remain unknown. Parameterized cost and explicitly provisional diagnostic thresholds are appropriate.",
    "DeepGEMM #452 merge status and exhaustive review coverage are unknown. For #303's slowdown report, hardware, exact workload, effect size and causal explanation remain unknown."
  ]
}
